  "note": "One config's kernel profile: sampling (plan_points.py, optional --reuse-capture), capture, census, ranking, selection; delivers kernels.json via stages/profile/finalize.py. c28 regression: preserve sampling-partition ownership in 2D bands; stable band IDs prevent colliding case IDs when owners share a cell. Planner validation and shared lock fixes are in brain/tools and stages/_shared. vLLM 0.33 (MiniMax-M3.1-Flash, TP4, DSpark, DBO): frontend traces kept out of ranks, engine-log server_info, valid eager prefix, multi-point eager windows, serial windows for DBO prefill, overlapped copies billed by exposed time, ROCclr runtime kernels as memory, amd_kernels entries as operators. Task boundaries and the UT request are the brain's (brain/README.md); brain/tools was removed. Request references point at the UT request contract. PR 643 records important shapes and per-case launch evidence. Keep important-cell planning cheap as in c6ec399. plan_points --important-cells caps the important cells per phase (default 24), recorded in sampling_plan.json.",
